<p style="color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem">
A wholesale clothing supplier is only as useful as its production range, and
that's where Bangladesh's factory base stands out: the same manufacturing
infrastructure that makes the country the world's second-largest garment
exporter also means one supplier can realistically cover knitwear, wovens,
activewear, and outerwear categories rather than specializing in just one.
</p>
<p style="color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem">
For wholesale buyers, that range translates into fewer supplier relationships
to manage across a catalog. SDF Clothing supplies across categories at a
300-piece-per-style minimum, holds GOTS and OEKO-TEX certification, and ships
EU orders duty-free under the GSP scheme — useful when a single purchase order
spans multiple garment types.
</p>
<p style="color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem">
Sourcing wholesale from Bangladesh means drawing on decades of built-out
capacity across fabric types and construction methods, rather than a factory
that's recently pivoted into apparel. Bulk lead times run 30 to 45 days across
most categories, and the Dhaka-Chittagong export corridor is built to consolidate
mixed-category shipments efficiently.
</p>
<p style="color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem">
Wholesale buyers reselling into the US avoid the Section 301 tariffs applied to
Chinese-origin apparel across nearly every category, while EU-bound wholesale
orders clear duty-free under GSP. Across a mixed catalog, that tariff gap
compounds — it applies to every SKU, not just one product line.
</p>
